# Code owners for OllamaMobile.
#
# GitHub applies the LAST matching pattern only, so the more specific entries
# below deliberately repeat @jaypetez rather than adding to the catch-all.
# Today there is a single maintainer; the split exists so that reviewer
# expectations are already encoded when more people show up, and so that
# high-risk paths are visibly marked as such.

*                       @jaypetez

# Native inference. Anything here can crash the process outside the JVM,
# leak memory the GC cannot reclaim, or change ABI/packaging of the shipped
# .so files. Highest blast radius in the repo.
/core-llm/              @jaypetez
/core-llm-api/          @jaypetez

# Vendored/third-party sources (llama.cpp submodule and friends). Changes
# here are licence-relevant as well as technical: llama.cpp is MIT and its
# attribution must survive any update.
/third_party/           @jaypetez

# CI, release automation, issue/PR templates. A bad change here is silent —
# it does not fail a build, it just stops a gate from running.
/.github/               @jaypetez

# Documentation.
/docs/                  @jaypetez
